| `scripts/resource_limits.py` | Starts a program with a time limit and an output cap (`run_bounded`), in a session of its own that it ends whole with SIGKILL when the child outlives the limit or writes past the cap, so a hung or flooding child cannot hold its caller; what the child left in its session is ended and named in a log warning, a process outside the session holding a pipe gets one shared 2-second drain window and is then named, not signalled, and the child's own status is returned. The child's session also ends when its caller gets a SIGTERM or SIGHUP it does not handle, when its caller is SIGKILLed (a watcher process ends it), and when a server returns after a stop signal; `scripts/run_make_target.py` runs make on the same supervisor. `run_tool` is the same runner under `agents.tool_timeout_seconds` and `agents.tool_max_output_bytes` (`tool_limits`), for every tool child an agent starts and the MCP action server's doer; it refuses a time limit shorter than the gate runner's own limit plus twice its stop grace plus `agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds`. Gives each server entry point a memory cap (`cap_memory`, RLIMIT_AS) and a named shutdown owner (`shutdown_owner`), so SIGTERM stops a server cleanly with exit 0. | imported by `models/claude_code_headless.py`, `api/rest_fastapi/serve.py`, `api/grpc/server.py`, `mcp/protocol.py`, `mcp/action_server.py` and the `_brain.py` of `agents/doc_reviewer`, `agents/index_enforcer`, `agents/practice_refactor` and `agents/wiki_navigator` | [`agents.tool_timeout_seconds`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`agents.tool_max_output_bytes`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`agents.tool_gate_margin_seconds`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`models.timeout_seconds.<adapter>`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`models.max_reply_bytes`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`transports.serve.memory_cap_mb`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`transports.serve.shutdown_grace_seconds`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | A process that calls setsid leaves the session and is not reached; off POSIX only the child itself is ended. The memory cap counts address space, not resident memory, and each child a server starts inherits its own copy rather than sharing it. Stdlib-only and 3.6-safe. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md) | always |
